    "note": "Module S1b (core/s1b_person_association.py), between S1 and S2: all YOLOX boxes -> RTMW each -> cross-view grouping -> 3D tracks -> locked target. Values set from geometry before any real-data run (2026-10-29), not tuned on MAMMA or AdvancedTake metrics. Gates: a camera joins a person if its median body-joint reprojection error <= max(floor, rel x box height); tracks match on the median body-joint distance to a constant-velocity prediction. capture_volume camera_ring = circle around the mean camera XY, radius = fraction x mean camera distance; auto_select locks only when exactly one person is inside it. Changed after the synthetic tests only (before any real-data run): rel gate 0.06 -> 0.03 and min_views_birth 3, because two people in line along one camera's ray gave 4-camera chimera groups with 10-26 px errors that passed a 0.06 gate.",
